            "notes": "**Power:**\nFor the first round we are going to want to take [Clone Conjuration](item_6c9f6be1-ab29-4f46-af24-34e4835f9af3) as it allows the Clone to farm cash. The Clone was recently reworked to allow it to gain cash from Healing and Damage but it does less. This is still a considerable amount more cash than if it was just you alone. \n_________\n**Items:**\nFor the items, we are going to pick up [Power Playbook](item_6d8803cf-baa7-46ee-af91-51e7f2301418) as it gives us more health to your clone which allows it to do more Damage and Healing whilst active. \n\nFor the survival items, we are going to pick up [Armored Vest](item_358361e2-59be-4c81-b221-8a87f37809e6) or [First Aid Kit](item_0172eaaa-1902-44a3-b989-d12f0f7301da) depending if you prefer Armour or Shields. However, you can also not bother with either of these items and instead pick up [Weapon Grease](item_961ae72f-434f-406b-a89b-ab8efec806bf) or [Compensator](item_2a354f80-610c-4661-9bdd-8960ae1a60b0) for a small buff to your Healing/Damage - this increases the clones healing/damage too. \n\nFor the final item, we are going to buy [Charged Plating](item_b8ca58e7-6ae2-40ee-8618-fe2f32315295) for the bonus Armour and Ability Power after using Kitsune Rush. This is just going to help us stay alive and keep the clone active.\n_______\n**Round Notes:**\nIt is imperative that you are using Swift Step as soon as it is available as it allows you to farm Stadium Cash and you can get ahead of all other players very quickly.",
