            "notes": "**Power:** The final power is very situational as the remaining powers are very strong in their own ways, However, I usually pick [Crossing Guard](item_bb5252fd-fc6b-4dce-a60a-21b0a0add68f) for the slow to enemies whilst Kitsune is active or [Fleet Foot](item_1d58371c-71a9-44c2-8d5a-0663467599e9) to be able to escape when you are alone. ***Important note:*** The [Fleet Foot](item_1d58371c-71a9-44c2-8d5a-0663467599e9) does have a 35% increased cooldown but this is negligible as this final build has -30% [Cooldown Reduction](stat_cooldown_reduction). \n\n[Spirit Veil](item_1772ce7d-37ed-41e4-8bac-d9b260aa59ad) is also a very strong choice if you find yourself using Kitsune more defensively. \n_____\n**Items:** We are going to purchase [Martian Mender](item_0099632b-4e18-450e-844f-22c40e51bc98) and [Our Bikes](item_d9fa8542-237e-49d5-b6a1-4e910d5c777f). [Our Bikes](item_d9fa8542-237e-49d5-b6a1-4e910d5c777f) is the most important item to purchase this round as it allows you to keep your team up even more when you have Kitsune active which should be **very** often. The [Martian Mender](item_0099632b-4e18-450e-844f-22c40e51bc98) is best for the additional [Cooldown Reduction](stat_cooldown_reduction) and Health, but you can switch this out for any other item that you like..\n_____\n**Round Notes:** For the final round, you should be able to comfortably be able to purchase six purple items with lots leftover.",
